  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I am not entirely sure how hard implementing this would be, but the general idea is to scan every animator on your avatar and detect which objects are affected by IsLocal animations. If they are ONLY visible locally, exclude them from the performance check.\n\nExample: I have a UI driven by contacts, hundreds of them to be exact. However, I created it to be local-only so that no one else can see it. However, the performance score is still very poor from the UI alone despite no one seeing it.\n\nAn even better idea would be to add a dynamic performance ranking system that not only checks for local-only objects but also those that are hidden. If I have, say, a gun with a bunch of fancy effects but haven't equipped it, the performance score should reflect that. When I pull the gun out, the performance score will automatically adjust to reflect it. This could also allow for dynamically showing and hiding avatars based on this with no user input.\n\nOn first glance, the user should see the minimum and maximum possible performance score that the avatar can have as two separate performance ranks.",
